# Copy to .env only if you need a machine-specific override.
#
# Normally you do NOT need a .env at all: the API target comes from the mode
# files, which are committed:
#   .env.development  npm run dev         -> http://127.0.0.1:8000
#   .env.remote       npm run dev:remote  -> https://talentpulseai-api.onrender.com
#   .env.production   npm run build       -> https://talentpulseai-api.onrender.com
#
# Never create .env.local / .env.development.local for this — they override every
# mode file at once and are the reason a "local" dev server can silently talk to
# the deployed API.
